nsider_own":0.00072999997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Brookfield Renewable Partners L.P. owns a portfolio of renewable power generating facilities in the North America, Colombia, and Brazil. The company generates electricity through hydroelectric, wind, solar, distributed generation, and pumped storage; and offers sustainable solutions, such as renewable natural gas, carbon capture and storage, recycling, cogeneration, biomass, nuclear services, eFuels, and power transformation. It operates as the general partner of Brookfield Renewable Partners L.P. The company was formerly known as Brookfield Renewable Energy Partners L.P. and changed its name to Brookfield Renewable Partners L.P. in May 2016. The company was founded in 1999 and is based in Toronto, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Connor David Teskey | Chief Executive Officer | Age 38 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $956K ranks in the below the sector median among Utilities peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Brookfield Renewable Partners L is a large-cap utilities business with a $21.3B market cap on $6.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","The company is burning through $5.4B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 1427% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 145% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4479623574447724},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Utilities peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to BEPC Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/139/Technical_Reactions_to_BEPC_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_110626071201_1794010321.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794010321.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Market Outlook: Strong earnings offer support after tech selloff","source":"bnnbloom